From 1a956468fa5751ba71a3b81be68a2273bf8ae294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:27:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(ui): move pixel snapshots to the release lane;
 structural UI tests in the PR suite

The three PNG golden tests (egui_shell_snapshot, egui_shell_snapshot_light,
tool_editor_snapshot) are #[ignore]d with a "release lane (#255)" reason
and run only in a new ui snapshot lane of the release tier (gate.ps1 and
gate.sh: debug, --lib --ignored snapshot, CWD crates/ui). Quick and batch
no longer read or write crates/ui/tests/snapshots/*.png.

Their intent is covered in the default suite by egui_app::tests::structural
(shell_structure_dark, shell_structure_light, tool_editor_structure):
AccessKit labels/roles/disabled state/window presence plus the painted
strips' text and coarse placement - text-only and platform independent.

AGENTS.md Testing, the PR-reviewer agent and the review-prs skill now say a
PR must not change snapshot PNGs; they are regenerated once at the cut.
#[test] count in crates/ui: 414 -> 417 (3 moved to ignored, 3 added).

Fixes #255

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
